From 139fb224202ca48bf3e6b9cf18ae5673fc565a08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rishxb-arch <270784950+Rishxb-arch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 22:36:53 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(extract): resolve self/this calls to the enclosing class

A file-wide label map let a later class's method win, so a self/this/bare
call inside Dog became an EXTRACTED edge to Cat's same-named method.
Same-class calls now use the method edges of the enclosing class. An
unrelated class in the file is left unresolved; a hit that is already an
ancestor is kept, and module-level functions still resolve.

Co-Authored-By: Grok 4.7 <noreply@x.ai>
